{number: 103}
{title: Anywhere with Jesus}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Anywhere with Jesus I can safely go,
[F] Anywhere He leads me in this world be-[C] low;
Anywhere without Him dearest [G7] joys would fade,
[C] Anywhere with Jesus [G7] I am not a-[C] fraid.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[F] Anywhere! Anywhere! [C] Fear I cannot know;
[G7] Anywhere with Jesus I can [C] safely go.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Anywhere with Jesus I need fear no ill,
[F] Tho' temptations gather round my pathway [C] still;
He Himself was tempted that He [G7] might help me;
[C] Anywhere with Jesus [G7] I may victor [C] be.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Anywhere with Jesus I am not alone;
[F] Other friends may fail me, He is still my [C] own;
Tho' His hand may lead me over [G7] dreary ways,
[C] Anywhere with Jesus [G7] is a house of [C] praise.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C] Anywhere with Jesus I can go to sleep,
[F] When the dark'ning shadows round about me [C] creep;
Knowing I shall waken, never [G7] more to roam,
[C] Anywhere with Jesus [G7] will be home, sweet [C] home.
{end_of_verse}
